    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="1440" n="1335" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg1335"/>

                <head>320. Letter From John Foster Dulles to
                        Eisenhower<anchor n="1" xml:id="d320-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-04-30">April 30, 1958</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Mr. President:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d320-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d320-1"/>
                <p>I enclose a summary record of the discussion last Saturday with Al Gruenther, Bob Lovett, Jack McCloy and
                        Bedell Smith. I am sending you
                    separately some recommendations about the question of testing.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">John Foster
                            Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d320-a1.xml" xpointer="d320-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d320-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d320-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Transmits a record of Dulles’ meeting with disarmament advisory panel.
                    Top Secret. 9 pp. Eisenhower Library, Whitman File, Dulles–Herter Series,
                    Disarmament.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
